# Space News Scraper Walkthrough

I have successfully implemented a Python-based scraper that fetches the latest news from space.com, extracts key details, saves them to a CSV file, and includes a scheduling mechanism.

## Features
- **Scraping**: Fetches news from `space.com/news`.
- **Extraction**: Captures Title, Author, Date, Synopsis, and URL.
- **Storage**: Appends new articles to [space_news.csv](file:///Users/bytedance/.gemini/antigravity/brain/a4525af3-cd4e-4070-8bc9-0d0174c8a02d/space_news.csv), avoiding duplicates.
- **Scheduling**: Can be configured to run daily (default set to 09:00 AM).

## Files
- [scraper.py](file:///Users/bytedance/.gemini/antigravity/brain/a4525af3-cd4e-4070-8bc9-0d0174c8a02d/scraper.py): The main script.
- [requirements.txt](file:///Users/bytedance/.gemini/antigravity/brain/a4525af3-cd4e-4070-8bc9-0d0174c8a02d/requirements.txt): Dependencies.
- [space_news.csv](file:///Users/bytedance/.gemini/antigravity/brain/a4525af3-cd4e-4070-8bc9-0d0174c8a02d/space_news.csv): Output file (generated after running).

## How to Run

1.  **Install Dependencies**:
    ```bash
    pip install -r requirements.txt
    ```

2.  **Run the Scraper**:
    ```bash
    python scraper.py
    ```
    The script will run immediately once to fetch the latest news, and then enter a loop to run daily at 09:00 AM. Press `Ctrl+C` to stop the scheduler.

## Verification Results

I ran the scraper and it successfully generated [space_news.csv](file:///Users/bytedance/.gemini/antigravity/brain/a4525af3-cd4e-4070-8bc9-0d0174c8a02d/space_news.csv).

### Sample Output ([space_news.csv](file:///Users/bytedance/.gemini/antigravity/brain/a4525af3-cd4e-4070-8bc9-0d0174c8a02d/space_news.csv))
```csv
title,author,published_date,synopsis,url,fetched_at
SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket streaks into Florida's night sky...,Mike Wall,2025-11-19T01:42:03Z,SpaceX launched another batch...,https://www.space.com/...,2025-11-19T11:22:19...
The Euclid space telescope observed 1.2 million galaxies...,Robert Lea,2025-11-18T23:00:00Z,The data is starting to reveal...,https://www.space.com/...,2025-11-19T11:22:19...
...
```

The scraper correctly handles:
- **Titles**: Extracted cleanly.
- **Authors**: "By" prefix removed.
- **Dates**: Extracted from `datetime` attribute.
- **Duplicates**: Checks existing URLs before adding.
